Pros;
Great concepts, great ideas.
Cons;
Poor implementation. Buggy UI. Intermittant crashes.
This game was praised to be Game of Kings the video game. Its not bad but I would not go that far by a mile.

{UPDATE}
The bugs have gone (afaik) and the DLC is great fun. Keep it up!
{OLD REVIEW}
Buggiest thing I have EVER played. Most of the units bug out, stare at walls, or plain an simply cannot find home and get angry and desert you (while standing 2 blocks off where they want to go).
Enemy units bug out, sink into the floor and cannot be attacked anymore, while they themselves are able to do so.
And please stop those useless Zerg levels. If I want to play StarCraft, I will gladly do so. At least with StarCraft I don't have to spam a Heal spell like it owes me money, just to fight 3 guys that can insta-spawn high level creatures en masse. While I have to constantly remake workers to claim something I could be using, maybe, if I'm lucky.

When I saw that this game will be realeased I thought that this game will be one of the best simulators I've ever played. Right now after playing 50+ hours I'm dissapointed.
Pros:
+ finally a Truck Simulator in America;
+ America looks amazing;
+ idea with fines - more you get - more you have to pay.
Cons:
- only 3 states;
- only 2 dealers;
- AI is so freakin' dumb;
- game looks like ETS 2, but in USA.
At the end I wanna tell you that I'LL STILL BE PLAYING THIS GAME, because I bought it, but right now I don't recommend to buy it...

First of all, I shall ignore all of the bugs, as the game is in its Alpha stage.
Here are some great features about this game:
– full nudity;
– player character models.
This game is (and ostensibly, will be) a parody for
, another game by Funcom. Basically, if you wish to play the game, you can do it for free in
by visiting a resource area (the Cimmerian End (for PVP), the Aquilonian End, and the Stygian end) and building a guild city there while fighting off wild life and other players.
The only big difference is that Conan Exiles has
– no combo or movement system, which makes combat as boring as it gets;
– no abilities for you and your enemies, which makes the combat easy and predicatable;
– no raids, no groups, no dungeons, and no challenge;
– no skill system like in
;
– stolen ("borrowed") models and textures from
.
Basically, this is a more "accessible game" (read: "silly"). If you are a fortunate individual who have played only for 2 hours or less, then you can still refund the game. Do it. Funcom is known for making games worse over time.
